export const termsHtml = "<h1>Foreman Terms of Service</h1>\n<p><strong>Effective date:</strong> July 17, 2026</p>\n<p><strong>Last updated:</strong> July 17, 2026</p>\n<p>These Terms of Service (&quot;Terms&quot;) are an agreement between you and <strong>Farris Industries</strong> (&quot;we,&quot; &quot;us,&quot; &quot;our&quot;), the operator of Foreman (&quot;the app,&quot; &quot;the service&quot;). By creating an account or using Foreman, you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use Foreman.</p>\n<blockquote><p><strong>The short version.</strong> Foreman is a coaching app for working managers. It gives you coaching support, not professional advice. You must be 18 or older. Paid subscriptions renew automatically until you cancel. You can cancel anytime and keep access through the end of your paid period, but payments already made are not refunded by us. Your privacy is covered in our <a href=\"/privacy\">Privacy Policy</a>.</p></blockquote>\n<h2>1. Who can use Foreman</h2>\n<p>You must be at least 18 years old to create an account and use Foreman. By using the service, you confirm that you are 18 or older and that the information you give us is accurate. You are responsible for keeping your login credentials secure and for activity that happens under your account.</p>\n<h2>2. What Foreman is, and what it is not</h2>\n<p>Foreman is a coaching tool. It helps you reflect on workplace situations and offers coaching-style responses generated with the help of AI. It is intended to support your own thinking and decisions.</p>\n<p>Foreman is <strong>not</strong> a substitute for professional advice. It does not provide legal, medical, psychological, financial, or human-resources advice, and its responses should not be treated as such. Coaching responses are generated in part by AI and may be incomplete or wrong. You are responsible for your own decisions and actions. For serious workplace, legal, health, or safety matters, consult a qualified professional. If you are in crisis or someone is in danger, contact your local emergency services.</p>\n<h2>3. Your content</h2>\n<p>You keep ownership of the content you write in Foreman, including your check-ins, situations, notes, and retros. You grant us the limited permission needed to store your content, display it back to you, and process it to provide the service, including sending your text to our AI provider to generate coaching responses. We describe exactly how your data is handled in our <a href=\"/privacy\">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>\n<p>You are responsible for what you write. Do not use Foreman to store or submit content that is unlawful, that infringes someone else's rights, or that you do not have the right to share.</p>\n<h2>4. Acceptable use</h2>\n<p>When using Foreman, you agree not to:</p>\n<ul><li>Break the law or use the service for any unlawful purpose.</li><li>Attempt to access accounts, data, or systems that are not yours.</li><li>Interfere with, overload, or disrupt the service, or bypass rate limits and security measures.</li><li>Reverse engineer, scrape, or copy the service except as the law expressly allows.</li><li>Use the service to build or train a competing product.</li><li>Resell or redistribute access to the service without our written permission.</li></ul>\n<p>We may suspend or terminate accounts that violate these Terms.</p>\n<h2>5. Subscriptions, billing, and cancellation</h2>\n<p><strong>Free trial.</strong> New accounts start with a 14-day free trial of the full app. No payment method is required for the trial, and nothing is charged when it ends — if you have not subscribed by then, your access is paused until you choose a plan.</p>\n<p>Foreman offers paid subscriptions. When you subscribe, you authorize us or the applicable app store to charge you the stated price on a recurring basis. <strong>Subscriptions renew automatically</strong> at the end of each billing period until you cancel. Prices may change; if they do, we will give you notice before the change applies to you, and the new price takes effect on your next renewal.</p>\n<p>You can cancel anytime. When you cancel, your subscription stays active until the end of the period you have already paid for, and it does not renew after that. <strong>Payments already made are not refunded by us</strong>, except where required by law.</p>\n<p>If you purchased your subscription through the Apple App Store or Google Play, that store manages your billing, renewals, and refunds under its own policies. Refund requests for those purchases must go through the store, and any refund the store grants is governed by the store's rules, not these Terms. To cancel a store-based subscription, use your Apple or Google account settings.</p>\n<p>Some offerings — for example cohort programs and one-on-one coaching sessions — are one-time purchases rather than subscriptions. They do not renew, and unless stated otherwise at purchase they follow the same refund approach as subscriptions.</p>\n<p>Canceling is not the same as deleting your account. Canceling keeps your access until the end of the period you paid for. <strong>Deleting your account takes effect immediately</strong>: any active subscription is canceled on the spot, your data is erased, and the remaining paid period is not refunded. The deletion process is described in our <a href=\"/privacy\">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>\n<p>Payments made directly to us are processed by Stripe. We do not see or store your full card details.</p>\n<h2>6. Availability and changes to the service</h2>\n<p>We work to keep Foreman available and reliable, but we do not guarantee that it will always be uninterrupted or error-free. We may update, change, or discontinue features over time. If we discontinue a paid feature you are actively paying for, we will handle it fairly, which may include a pro-rated credit or refund for the unused paid portion where appropriate.</p>\n<h2>7. Third-party services</h2>\n<p>Foreman relies on third-party providers to operate, including Anthropic (AI responses), Stripe (payments), Supabase (database and authentication), Resend (email), Cloudflare (hosting), and Upstash (rate limiting). Your use of the service is also subject to the terms of the applicable app store. We are not responsible for the acts or omissions of these third parties, though we choose them carefully and describe their role in our Privacy Policy.</p>\n<h2>8. Disclaimers</h2>\n<p>Foreman is provided &quot;as is&quot; and &quot;as available,&quot; without warranties of any kind, whether express or implied, to the fullest extent permitted by law. We do not warrant that the service will meet your requirements, that coaching responses will be accurate or suitable for your situation, or that the service will be secure or error-free.</p>\n<h2>9. Limitation of liability</h2>\n<p>To the fullest extent permitted by law, Farris Industries will not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for any loss of data, profits, or goodwill, arising from your use of Foreman. Our total liability for any claim relating to the service is limited to the amount you paid us for the service in the twelve months before the claim arose, or one hundred dollars, whichever is greater. Some jurisdictions do not allow certain limitations, so parts of this section may not apply to you.</p>\n<h2>10. Termination</h2>\n<p>You may stop using Foreman and delete your account at any time, as described in our Privacy Policy. We may suspend or terminate your access if you violate these Terms or if we are required to by law. If your account is terminated, the sections of these Terms that by their nature should survive, including content ownership, disclaimers, and limitation of liability, will continue to apply.</p>\n<h2>11. Changes to these Terms</h2>\n<p>We may update these Terms as Foreman changes. If we make a material change, we will announce it, for example by email or an in-app notice, before it takes effect. Your continued use of the service after a change means you accept the updated Terms. The effective date at the top always reflects the current version.</p>\n<h2>12. Governing law</h2>\n<p>These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of Utah, without regard to its conflict-of-laws rules. Any dispute relating to these Terms or the service will be resolved in the state or federal courts located in Utah, and you agree to that jurisdiction, except where applicable law gives you the right to bring a claim elsewhere.</p>\n<h2>13. Contact</h2>\n<p>Questions about these Terms: cfarriscoaching@gmail.com, Farris Industries.</p>\n<p>See also our <a href=\"/privacy\">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>";
